# EXPECT: used after its loop in an observed/traced program
#
# Round 65: module-scope for binders are loop-scoped by the VM in EVERY
# regime, but observed/traced module emission routes the binder through
# the env -- the C block-scope mechanism is regime-gated -- where it
# SURVIVES the loop: `for i in [7, 8]: print of i / print of i` printed
# the phantom 8, rc 0, where the VM raises rc 1. Binders are correctly
# absent from g_module_names, so no membership-keyed guard could catch
# it; the shape refuses by name when the binder is used after its loop.
# A later `for` REBINDING the same name is a fresh scope and does NOT
# count as a use (the reuse idiom stays in the envelope).
#
# Envelope shape: the VM RUNS this (rc 0 -- the post-loop use sits in a
# dead if arm, so no leaked read ever executes).

x is 1
print of (report of x)
for i in [7, 8]:
    print of i
if 1 == 2:
    print of i
print of "done"
